  ── Per-pair results ────────────────────────

  Comparison                t (df)              p (raw)    p (adj)    d
  Alto vs Mezzo             -1.079 (14.00)      .299       .897       -0.539
  Alto vs Soprano           -2.128 (14.00)      .052       .155       -1.064
  Mezzo vs Soprano          -1.107 (14.00)      .287       .860       -0.554
  * adjusted p < 0.05. t and d both run first group minus second; d is Cohen's d.


  ── Adjusted p-values (Bonferroni) ──────────

              Alto        Mezzo       Soprano     
Alto          ---         .897        .155        
Mezzo         .897        ---         .860        
Soprano       .155        .860        ---         
  Symmetric: the p for A vs B is the p for B vs A.
  * adjusted p < 0.05


  ── Cohen's d (effect sizes) ────────────────

              Alto        Mezzo       Soprano     
Alto          ---         -0.539      -1.064      
Mezzo         0.539       ---         -0.554      
Soprano       1.064       0.554       ---         
  Row minus column: a negative d means the ROW group's mean is
  lower than the COLUMN group's. |d| is the effect size.

  Conventions: quartiles R type 7 · SD & variance n-1
  · rank tests average tied ranks (tie-corrected).
